  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\nRefresh on 2026-11-18 (merge of main `ed4a9940f`, head `56fa6694b`). The PR now keeps only caches whose key is the input itself (crates/ui/AGENTS.md, \"Frame cost\"):\r\n\r\n- `crates/ui/src/frame_cache.rs`: each body's world-space vertices. The key is the facet allocation (`Weak<[Triangle]>`, compared by pointer, plus the length) and the pose bits. `world::world_verts` uses it.\r\n- `crates/ui/src/pick_highlight.rs` (`HighlightCache`): the resolved outlines of the shown picks, the viewport hover and the Geometry-row hover. The key is the same as the key of `pick_line_memo`: the picks by value, and for each picked body its display-off flag, entity, `Arc<Features>` allocation and view pose.\r\n- `crates/ui/src/pick_highlight_mesh.rs`: each highlight layer is one cached `egui::Shape::Mesh` in `pick_ink::paint` and in the row hover of `shell::viewport_panel`. Each of the three slots (selected, viewport hover, row hover) is a `MeshSlot` with its own build counter. A cache hit sends a clone of the `Arc<Mesh>`, not a deep copy.\r\n- `crates/geometry/src/geometry/feature.rs`: `digest_of` uses a fixed array, not a heap `Vec` for each triangle (the same hash). `patches` and `patch_rings` build the lattice one time.\r\n- `crates/app/src/model/toolpath.rs`: `toolpath_nonempty` reads without a clone (`model.rs` only re-exports it). `operation::stamp::status_of` uses it. `toolpath_warning_count` had no caller and is removed.\r\n\r\nThe refresh removed these parts of the PR, because main has input-keyed memos for the same work, or because the key was a document counter:\r\n\r\n- `feature/index.rs` (`*_arc` helpers): main has `model::resolve_chain`, `model::patches` and `model::patch_rings`.\r\n- `SHARED_FEATURES_CACHE`: main has the Weak memo in `model::features_of`.\r\n- The scene, region and toolpath-line caches: main has `frame_memo::scene_scope` and `pick_line_memo`.\r\n- `panel_cache.rs` (six panel caches) and `History::revision_token`: keyed by a document counter.\r\n\r\n`docs/decisions/2201-highlighter-frame-perf.md` records each choice.\r\n\r\n## Cause\r\n\r\n- `pick_ink::paint` and `shell::viewport_panel` sent two `Shape::LineSegment` shapes for each projected segment in each frame.\r\n- The highlight outlines and the world vertices were built again in each frame when no input changed.\r\n\r\n## Screenshots\r\n\r\nThe refresh is a performance change only. It adds no new visible change. The screenshots of the original change are on the fork's `pr-screenshots` branch:\r\n\r\n| State | Before | After |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Selected edges | ![Before selected edges](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/3441230386b638c8bfd4478b8cb22b908ff25aad/2256/before-selected-edges.png) | ![After selected edges](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/3441230386b638c8bfd4478b8cb22b908ff25aad/2256/after-selected-edges.png) |\r\n| Hovered edge | ![Before hovered edge](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/3441230386b638c8bfd4478b8cb22b908ff25aad/2256/before-hovered-edge.png) | ![After hovered edge](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/3441230386b638c8bfd4478b8cb22b908ff25aad/2256/after-hovered-edge.png) |\r\n| Welded face | ![Before welded face](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/3441230386b638c8bfd4478b8cb22b908ff25aad/2256/before-welded-face.png) | ![After welded face](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/3441230386b638c8bfd4478b8cb22b908ff25aad/2256/after-welded-face.png) |\r\n\r\n## Tests\r\n\r\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/highlight_perf.rs` (4 tests):\r\n  - `three_selected_edge_pieces_draw_as_a_single_batched_highlight`\r\n  - `selected_highlight_builds_once_at_selection_and_zero_times_across_orbit_idle_and_hover`\r\n  - `selected_welded_patch_draws_as_batched_highlight_with_single_build`\r\n  - `dense_45k_model_with_multiple_ops_and_many_limit_findings_stays_stable_across_frames`\r\n- `crates/ui/src/pick_highlight_tests.rs` (new, counter and changed-input pins):\r\n  - `highlight_still_frames_build_the_outline_once`\r\n  - `highlight_rebuilds_when_the_pose_moves`\r\n  - `highlight_rebuilds_when_the_facets_are_replaced`\r\n  - `highlight_rebuilds_when_the_body_is_hidden_or_the_pick_changes`\r\n  - `viewport_hover_still_frames_build_once_and_a_new_feature_builds_again` (new: the viewport hover has its own counter, `hover_builds`; the row hover counts in `row_hover_builds`)\r\n- `crates/ui/src/pick_highlight_mesh_tests.rs` (new, screen-mesh cache pins, each test runs all three slots):\r\n  - `highlight_mesh_still_frames_tessellate_once_in_each_slot`\r\n  - `highlight_mesh_rebuilds_after_an_orbit_and_the_vertices_move`\r\n  - `highlight_mesh_rebuilds_after_a_pane_resize_and_the_vertices_move`\r\n  - `highlight_mesh_rebuilds_after_an_ink_change_and_the_colour_changes`\r\n- `crates/ui/src/frame_cache_tests.rs`:\r\n  - `world_verts_cached_does_not_reuse_stale_entry_after_source_release`\r\n  - `world_collect_rebuilds_vertices_when_model_facets_are_replaced`\r\n  - `world_collect_still_frames_transform_no_vertex_and_a_pose_change_does` (new)\r\n- The `#[test]` count of `crates/ui` goes up (this push adds 5). No test is deleted or ignored. No snapshot PNG changes.\r\n\r\n## Gate on `56fa6694b`\r\n\r\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` falls back to batch (876 steps), because `feature.rs` is in the diff. Thus the touched binaries ran one by one, in debug, on head `56fa6694b` (main `ed4a9940f` merged):\r\n\r\n- `camcraft-ui` lib (working directory `crates/ui`): 1175 passed, 0 failed, 7 ignored (the existing snapshot tests). This includes `highlight_perf`, `pick_highlight::tests`, `pick_highlight_mesh::tests` and `frame_cache::tests`.\r\n- `camcraft-app` lib: 368 passed, 1 ignored.\r\n- `camcraft-geometry` lib: 49 passed.\r\n- `camcraft-app` suites `stock_stamp` (4), `stale_rapid_law` (2), `wire_stamp` (7), `carried_verify` (8), `feature_edge_g1_join` (5), `vertex_pick` (4): all pass.\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-geometry -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\r\n\r\n## Goldens moved\r\n\r\n- None.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- The `SLOW_BINARIES` of the release tier.\r\n- Live GPU frame timing in a windowed session.\r\n- The other `camcraft-app` and `camcraft-ui` integration suites (the batch tier runs them after the merge).\r\n- Review non-blockers left open: the vertex cache keeps one entry for each pose (bounded at 32), the vertex cache hit clones the vertex vector, and the law tests of `interact::hover_features` use `pick_highlight::project_segments`, not the production projection.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Cache the pick highlight outlines and the world vertices by their inputs, and draw each viewport pick highlight as one batched mesh.\r\n\r\nFixes #2201\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n",
